{"availability":"available","full":"imamhamid/kana-dojo-react","name":"kana-dojo-react","description":"Best Kana Trainer App 2026: Learn Hiragana and Katakana Fast","category":"Education","language":"HTML","stars":56,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-21T21:37:19Z","updated":"2026-10-08T06:54:32Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["hiragana","japanese-characters","kana-trainer","katakana","reactjs","trainer"],"demo":"https://imamhamid.github.io/kana-dojo-react/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:34:36.301Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T07:34:36.301Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T07:34:36.301Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T07:34:36.301Z","stars":56,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["KanaFlow is a next-generation, browser-native learning environment for mastering hiragana and katakana — the twin syllabaries that form the rhythmic backbone of written Japanese. Instead of treating memorization as a chore, KanaFlow turns stroke recognition, sound recall, and reading fluency into a flowing, adaptive experience that adjusts to your pace, your mistakes, and your momentum.","Born from the spirit of open-source language tooling and refined for the 2026 web platform, KanaFlow is a single-page React application that runs entirely in the client. No accounts, no servers phoning home, no tracking pixels — just you, 46 base characters, their dakuten and handakuten cousins, and the delightful combo forms that make Japanese reading click into place.","Most kana trainers behave like flashcards glued to a wall. You flip, you guess, you forget, you repeat. KanaFlow was designed around a different metaphor: a river of characters. Each glyph you learn is a stone you place into the riverbed. As the stones accumulate, the current of reading becomes smoother, faster, and eventually second nature."],"features":["🎴 Adaptive Spaced Repetition — a lightweight SM-2-inspired scheduler that quietly decides when each kana should reappear.","🖌️ Stroke Order Animations — SVG-based stroke sequences that replay smoothly and can be scrubbed frame by frame.","🔊 Native Pronunciation Playback — clearly recorded or synthesized audio for every base character and combination.","⌨️ Typing Trainer — romaji-to-kana input drills that build muscle memory for real keyboards.","🧠 Confusion Matrix — a heatmap showing which kana you mix up most often (し vs つ, ソ vs ン, and other classic traps)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/imamhamid/kana-dojo-react/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"25e94c394e3f42cf68df07c113c19c745950ad33b899d5ac63a9bb5058b92cb5","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T07:34:36.485Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:34:36.485Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"KanaFlow is a next-generation, browser-native learning environment for mastering hiragana and katakana — the twin syllabaries that form the rhythmic backbone of written Japanese. Instead of treating memorization as a chore, KanaFlow turns stroke recognition, sound recall, and reading fluency into a flowing, adaptive experience that adjusts to your pace, your mistakes, and your momentum.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/imamhamid/kana-dojo-react/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"No accounts, no servers phoning home, no tracking pixels — just you, 46 base characters, their dakuten and handakuten cousins, and the delightful combo forms that make Japanese reading click into place.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/imamhamid/kana-dojo-react/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Do I need an account?","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/imamhamid/kana-dojo-react/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"25e94c394e3f42cf68df07c113c19c745950ad33b899d5ac63a9bb5058b92cb5","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/imamhamid/kana-dojo-react/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T07:34:36.486Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T06:54:3